        "GradTS consists of three successive modules responsible for (1) ranking attention heads for a task based on their contributions, (2) ranking auxiliary tasks based on inter-task correlations, and (3) finalizing the auxiliary task sets, respectively.\n",
        "\\subsection{Attention Head Ranking Module}\n",
        "We estimate the importance of attention heads to a task using the absolute gradients accumulated at each head, following \\citet{head-importance-1}.\n",
        "Specifically, we achieve the goal in four steps:\n",
        "(1) We fine-tune a pre-trained Transformer-based model on a task.\n",
